  "assessment": [
    "Two independent literal UDP request/response exchanges, distinct upstream sockets and actual published receiver task IDs precede controlled read faults. Each original fault is consumed by the existing actual Pending receive wrapper; both real task completion/destruction precede stop_relay. No collector outcome is retrieved by the test before the canonical stop.",
    "External cancellation aborts the actual published receiver only after literal traffic and Pending observations. Actual handle completion and receiver destruction precede canonical stop; returned JoinError cancellation/id are downstream target assertions, not independently harvested or fabricated values.",
    "Per-client observation state is registered before child spawn; actual JoinSet AbortHandle is published synchronously before the coordinator yields. Observer mode is opt-in, default false. None and prior default-observer operations reverse exactly to af830.",
    "ReceiverBackup exists before all fallible acquisitions. It delegates finite outer backup, then reads all retained receiver handles, aborts and finitely observes completion. Poison and original Elapsed remain composed with primary failure. AbortHandle observations do not steal JoinSet results.",
    "A successful outer backup establishes parent terminal publication before the final registry snapshot. If outer backup times out, its error remains and no frozen-publication or all-descendants completion claim follows. Drop requests abort and reports poison; it does not join.",
    "Existing unit receiver silently returns on read error and original stop suppresses its own outer cancellation. The intended baseline leaves these defects unchanged rather than manufacturing expected error objects."
  ],
  "forecasts": [
    {
      "method": "stopping_a_relay_retains_both_completed_receiver_failures",
